(OPR-23: LANGUAGE.md:4861 lists `aren't` as an accepted spelling of `not`.
 On 0.4.9 and earlier it failed for the same lexical reason as OPR-22.
 See Discrepancy 1. `aren't` stands for the plural `are not`
 (LANGUAGE.md:1972), so the witness needs a plural predicate that is
 actually true: `lhs` (7) and `rhs` (9) are both `aren't 3`.
